the WNBA and were expected to be strong, although they lost one of their top players, " [:a {:href "/athletes/2102733"} "Katie Lou Samuelson"] ", to a positive COVID-19 test shortly before the tournament."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Basketball 3x3 consisted of games to 21 points, or to the highest score in 10 minutes of play, with sudden-death if tied at the end of regulation time. Teams had 3 players with one substitute allowed. A very fast-paced game, a 12-second shot clock was in play for the offensive team."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/18000000"} "3x3 Basketball, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "24 – 28 July 2021"] "\n" [:td {} "32"] "\n" [:td {} "8"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/18000039"} "3x3 Basketball, Women"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "24 – 28 July 2021"] "\n" [:td {} "32"] "\n" [:td {} "8"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n64 (32/32)\n"] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n13 (8/8)\n"] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n\n\n" [:h2 {} "Medals"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {:colspan "2"} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] "\n" [:th {:colspan "2"} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] "\n" [:th {:colspan "2"} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {:class "top"} [:a {:href "/results/18000000"} "3x3 Basketball, Men"]] "\n" [:td {:style "vertical-align: top"} "Latvia"] [:td {:style "vertical-align: top"} [:a {:href "/countries/LAT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/LAT.png"}] "LAT"]] "\n" [:td {:style "vertical-align: top"}